# Phase 18 Producer runtime backpressure/retry parity — 2026-10-13

- Starting revision: `c1475a78` on `phase/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate`; worktree was clean. The pinned Java source checkout was read-only and remains at commit `2238256de1d227a4384ba969dfa31473187b4d08` with its pre-existing untracked `broker/src/test/java/org/apache/rocketmq/broker/aaaa.java` preserved.
- Implemented runtime async backpressure enable/count/byte getters and setters on `Producer`. A fair weighted adjustable semaphore preserves in-flight permits during capacity changes, including negative available capacity after a reduction below current use. Runtime config getters expose updated values. Added Rust equivalents for Java's inside-adjust fields and RAII read-lock guards.
- Added a live `RetryResponseCodes` handle returned by `ProducerConfig` and `Producer`, with add/remove/clear/extend/retain/snapshot behavior. Retry decisions read the shared set; cloned `ProducerConfig` values keep independent snapshots.
- Extended the invoked Java Producer fixture for runtime backpressure settings and live retry-code-set mutations. Reflected the Java semaphore to record permit preservation: 7 in flight, 5 available after changing limit 1024→12, then 12 available after completion. Fixture SHA-256: `a6dcc14b5bf14cf1a00c4f5c6cb970c8255d20637fa7b2304cf196be7a0c47cc`.
- PASS: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-producer --locked` (107 unit tests plus admin, Producer, request/reply, scripted-send and transaction integrations); focused backpressure/retry/fixture tests; `cargo clippy -p rocketmq-classic-producer -p rocketmq-classic --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings`; `cargo fmt --all -- --check`; `git diff --check`; `mvn -q -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` (37 scenarios and fixture drift checks).
- Updated the Phase 6 audit, Phase 7 Producer matrix and release checklist. Code and documentation commits are pending. Remaining P18-V01 work includes public compressor/accumulator mapping, the broader Java reverse-export/source/input/branch audit, and any other gaps found by it. Full workspace gates and required GitHub Ubuntu evidence remain pending; Phase 19 Broker/Docker work remains future validation.
- Code commit: `b9d01c43` (`feat(producer): add runtime async control parity`). Documentation and this log are being committed separately.

# P18-V01 Producer compressor/accumulator API mapping — 2026-10-13

- Starting revision: `d0086880`; code commit: `d56e4094` (`feat(producer): map compressor and accumulator APIs`). Java reference checkout remained read-only.
- Added public `ProducerCompressor` snapshots with `compress`/`decompress`, runtime `Producer::set_compress_type`, accumulator initialization state and runtime auto-batch accessors. `Producer::start` initializes the accumulator at Java's source-backed startup point; later auto-batch toggles affect subsequent sends. `ProducerConfig` clones remain detached snapshots for these settings.
- Extended the invoked Java Producer fixture for all three compressor implementations and retained-object behavior after type replacement, plus auto-batch getter results before initialization and after runtime toggles. Fixture SHA-256: `da417c35e77ed3c6c8edff59ea226d8fd4e9607f43a6eef085889223dfe1d3ec`.
- The first fixture-generation Maven run exposed missing `throws Exception` on the fixture builder; corrected the declaration and reran. PASS: `mvn -q -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml -Dproducer.core.fixture.verify=false verify`; final fixture drift check: `mvn -q -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` (37 scenarios, fixture drift checks and Java/Rust cross-decodes).
- PASS: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-producer --locked` (107 unit tests; 38 integration tests across admin, producer, request/reply, scripted-send and transaction); strict producer/facade all-target/all-feature Clippy; `cargo fmt --all -- --check`; `git diff --check`; `cargo build -p rocketmq-classic --examples --release --locked`.
- Updated Phase 6 audit, Phase 7 Producer matrix and release checklist in a separate documentation commit. P18-V01 remains open for Java reverse exports, inherited/trait APIs and source/input/branch reconciliation. The full workspace gate on the latest Producer revision, current GitHub Ubuntu evidence, and Phase 19 Docker/Broker scenarios remain pending; the deployment-only manual checklist is separate.

